    "type": "service",
    "title": "LIS-like Snow Cover Fraction",
    "description": "Snow cover fraction (number of snow dates divided by the number of clear dates) and number of clear observations from Sentinel-2 L2A, with a simplified version of the CNES/CESBIO Let-it-snow (LIS) algorithm: pass 1 (NDSI > n1 and red > r1), pass 2 above a snowline elevation (NDSI > n2 and red > r2) with the Copernicus DEM GLO-30, pass 3 for snow in relief self-shadow (LIS hillshade from slope, aspect and the sun angles of each date, and blue - NIR > shaded_snow_pass), and a Sen2Cor SCL cloud and no-data mask. Original implementation inspired by Gascoin et al. (2019), ESSD 11, 493-514.",
